{"mitigating_catastrophic_forgetting": "Mitigating Catastrophic Forgetting refers to strategies and techniques aimed at preventing the loss of previously acquired knowledge when a model learns new information. This is a critical challenge in machine learning, especially in the context of continually evolving models.|Here is another description: Mitigating Catastrophic Forgetting refers to the process of reducing or preventing the loss of previously acquired knowledge when a model learns new information. This is a critical challenge in machine learning, especially in the context of continually evolving large language models.|Here is another description: Mitigating Catastrophic Forgetting refers to strategies and techniques aimed at preventing the loss of previously acquired knowledge when training machine learning models, particularly in the context of continual learning.|Here is another description: Mitigating Catastrophic Forgetting refers to techniques aimed at preventing the loss of previously learned information when a machine learning model is trained on new data. This is a critical challenge in the development of large language models, which need to continually learn and adapt without forgetting prior knowledge."},
