{"superior_or_comparable_performance_compared_to_the_conventional_rehearsal_based_approaches_with_higher_data_utilization_efficiency": "The object describes the outcome of SSR's application, which is \"superior or comparable performance compared to the conventional rehearsal-based approaches, with higher data utilization efficiency.\" This means that SSR either matches or exceeds the performance of traditional methods while making better use of the available data."},
{"experiments": "The experiments refer to a series of tests and evaluations conducted to assess the performance and effectiveness of a specific approach or method, in this case, SSR (Synthetic Instance Selection and Rehearsal), in preserving the capabilities of large language models (LLMs).|Here is another description: The experiments refer to a series of studies and tests performed to evaluate and analyze various aspects of a system or model. In this context, the experiments are specifically designed to assess the performance and capabilities of a model under different conditions and tasks.|Here is another description: The experiments refer to a series of studies conducted on the SuperNI dataset, specifically designed to evaluate instruction tuning across various tasks and domains.|Here is another description: The experiments refer to a series of tests or studies conducted to evaluate a specific aspect or property.|Here is another description: The experiments refer to a series of studies or tests conducted to evaluate specific aspects of a system or model. In this context, the experiments are focused on understanding and improving the performance of a particular model."},
{"experiments__are_conducted_on__alpacaeval_and_mmlu_hendrycks_et_al_2021": "The phrase \"are conducted on\" indicates the action of performing experiments using specific datasets or benchmarks to evaluate the effectiveness and generalization capabilities of the approach being studied."},
{"alpacaeval_and_mmlu_hendrycks_et_al_2021": "AlpacaEval and MMLU (Hendrycks et al., 2021) are datasets or benchmarks used to evaluate the performance of language models. AlpacaEval likely refers to a specific evaluation dataset designed to test various aspects of language model performance, while MMLU (Massive Multitask Language Understanding) is a comprehensive benchmark introduced by Hendrycks et al. in 2021 to assess the multitask learning capabilities of language models across a wide range of subjects."},
{"ssr__can_effectively_preserve__the_generalization_capabilities_of_llms_in_general_domains": "The phrase \"can effectively preserve\" indicates SSR's capability to maintain or uphold a certain quality or performance level. In this context, it refers to SSR's ability to sustain the desired characteristics or functionalities of LLMs despite changes or updates."},
