{"instances": "The instances refer to individual data points or examples within the SuperNI dataset that are utilized for the purpose of training machine learning models. These instances are part of a subset of 10 tasks selected from the larger SuperNI dataset for continual learning experiments.|Here is another description: The instances refer to individual data points or examples within the chosen subset of 10 tasks from the SuperNI dataset. These instances are utilized for training and evaluation purposes in the continual learning experiments."},
{"instances__sampled_for_training__2_000": "The predicate \"sampled for training\" indicates the process by which a specific number of instances are randomly selected from the dataset to be used in the training phase of machine learning models. This selection is crucial for ensuring that the models learn effectively from a representative sample of the data."},
