{"kmeanssel_r": "KMeansSel(r) is a method that uses K-means clustering to group data into clusters and select a subset for training machine learning models. It serves as a baseline for comparison in various contexts, including continual learning tasks and selection processes, where its performance is evaluated against other methods like SSR and RandSel(r)."},
{"kmeanssel_r__employs__k_means_clustering_to_group_real_instances_into_20_clusters": "The predicate \"employs\" indicates that KMeansSel(r) utilizes or incorporates a specific technique or algorithm as part of its process. In this context, it refers to the use of K-means clustering as a step in the KMeansSel(r) method."},
{"k_means_clustering_to_group_real_instances_into_20_clusters": "K-means clustering is a popular unsupervised machine learning algorithm used to partition a dataset into distinct, non-overlapping subgroups (clusters) where each data point belongs to the cluster with the nearest mean. In the context of KMeansSel(r), it is used to group real instances into 20 clusters before making selections."},
{"kmeanssel_r__selects__instances_from_the_clusters": "The predicate \"selects\" in this context refers to the action of choosing or picking out specific elements from a set. In the case of KMeansSel(r), it denotes the process of making selections from the clusters formed by the K-means algorithm."},
{"instances_from_the_clusters": "Instances from the clusters refer to the individual data points that have been grouped together based on their characteristics and similarities as determined by the K-means clustering algorithm. These instances are the end results of the clustering process and are subject to further selection by the KMeansSel(r) method."},
{"training": "Training refers to the process of teaching a machine learning model, in this case, Large Language Models (LLMs), to improve its performance on a given task through the use of a dataset."},
{"training__utilize__lora_hu_et_al_2021_with_query_and_value_projection_matrices_in_the_self_attention_module": "Utilize means to make use of a specific method or tool in the training process. Here, it indicates the adoption of LoRA with specific modifications in the self-attention module to enhance the training of LLMs."},
{"lora_hu_et_al_2021_with_query_and_value_projection_matrices_in_the_self_attention_module": "LoRA (Hu et al., 2021) with query and value projection matrices in the self-attention module is a technique used to efficiently fine-tune large models by introducing low-rank adaptations. It involves modifying the query and value projection matrices within the self-attention mechanism to reduce the number of parameters that need to be updated during training."},
{"lora_rank": "LoRA rank refers to the rank of the Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) matrices used in the training of large language models (LLMs). It is a parameter that determines the complexity and adaptability of the model during the training process."},
{"lora_rank__set_to__8": "The predicate \"set to\" indicates the action of assigning a specific value or configuration to a parameter within the model's training setup. In this context, it means configuring the LoRA rank to a particular value."},
