{"dropout_rate": "The dropout rate refers to the proportion of neurons that are randomly omitted during the training of a neural network to prevent overfitting. In this context, it is a hyperparameter that influences the model's learning process."},
{"dropout_rate__set_to__0_1": "The phrase \"set to\" indicates the assignment of a specific value to a parameter within the model's configuration. In this case, it describes the action of configuring the dropout rate to a particular level."},
