{"adam_optimizer": "The Adam optimizer is a popular optimization algorithm used in machine learning and deep learning to update network weights iteratively based on training data. It combines the advantages of two other extensions of stochastic gradient descent: AdaGrad and RMSProp."},
{"adam_optimizer__employed_with__an_initial_learning_rate_of_2e_4": "The phrase \"employed with\" indicates that the Adam optimizer is being used in conjunction with a specific configuration or parameter setting during the training process of machine learning models."},
