{"icl": "ICL, or In-Context Learning, is a method used in the context of training large language models (LLMs) where a small subset of data is used to guide the model's learning process during training.|Here is another description: ICL, or In-Context Learning, is a method used in machine learning where the model learns from examples provided within the context of the task itself, rather than through extensive pre-training. In this scenario, ICL is applied in a sequence of continual learning tasks.|Here is another description: ICL, or In-Context Learning, is a method used in the continual learning process where a model is trained sequentially on different tasks. In this context, ICL is applied after training on the Alpaca52k dataset and before other tasks like QA, QG, SA, Sum., and Trans."},
{"icl__utilizes__1_of_the_training_data_from_superni_tasks_as_demonstrations": "The predicate \"utilizes\" indicates that ICL makes use of a specific amount of data from a designated source to enhance its learning capabilities. In this case, it refers to the process of incorporating a small percentage of training data into the model's learning process."},
{"1_of_the_training_data_from_superni_tasks_as_demonstrations": "1% of the training data from SuperNI tasks as demonstrations refers to a small subset of the overall training dataset used in the SuperNI tasks. This subset is specifically selected to serve as examples or demonstrations to aid in the in-context learning process of the language model."},
{"demonstrations__are__k_2": "The predicate \"are\" in this context signifies the quantity or number of demonstrations utilized. It indicates that a specific number of demonstrations are being considered for the ICL process."},
{"k_2": "_K_ = 2 denotes the specific number of demonstrations being used in the In-Context Learning process. In this case, two demonstrations are selected from the 1% of the training data from SuperNI tasks to aid in the model\u2019s learning and performance evaluation."},
