{"model_performance": "Model performance in this context refers to how well a machine learning model can make accurate predictions or classifications. It is a critical metric for evaluating the effectiveness and reliability of the model in practical applications.|Here is another description: Model performance refers to the effectiveness and efficiency of a machine learning model in making accurate predictions or classifications. In this context, it is evaluated based on the impact of using different rehearsal data percentages.|Here is another description: Model performance refers to how well a machine learning model can make accurate predictions or classifications on new, unseen data. It is typically measured using various metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, and F1 score, and is influenced by factors like the quality and representativeness of the training data."},
{"model_performance__when_using__r_1": "When using signifies the condition under which the model performance is assessed. It indicates that the performance metrics are observed specifically in scenarios where a certain percentage of rehearsal data is applied."},
