{"data_representativeness": "Data representativeness refers to the degree to which a dataset accurately reflects the variability and characteristics of the real-world scenarios it is intended to model. In machine learning, ensuring that the training data is representative is crucial for developing models that generalize well to new, unseen data."},
{"data_representativeness__demonstrating_the_importance_of__model_performance": "Demonstrating the importance of highlights the critical role that a particular factor plays in achieving a desired outcome. In this context, it emphasizes how crucial data representativeness is for influencing model performance, especially when the dataset is limited."},
