{"llms_such_as_llama_2_7b_and_alpaca_7b": "The object specifies the types of large language models (LLMs) that are being compared, namely Llama-2-7b and Alpaca-7b. These models are examples of advanced natural language processing systems that are often evaluated based on their performance metrics."},
{"ssr__evaluate__10_superni_tasks": "The predicate \"evaluate\" signifies the process of assessing or testing the performance and effectiveness of SSR against a set of tasks. This evaluation is crucial for determining how well SSR performs in comparison to other methods."},
{"10_superni_tasks": "The 10 SuperNI tasks represent a specific set of challenges or benchmarks used to test the capabilities of continual learning methods like SSR. These tasks are designed to measure different aspects of performance, such as accuracy retention (AR) and backward transfer (BWT).|Here is another description: The 10 SuperNI tasks represent a set of specific natural language processing challenges or benchmarks that are used to evaluate the performance of language models like Llama-2-7b."},
