{"ssr_with_llama_2_7b": "SSR with Llama-2-7b is a continual learning method that uses the Llama-2-7b model as its base language model. It is evaluated in a series of continual learning tasks to assess its performance over time.|Here is another description: SSR with Llama-2-7b is a method or system that utilizes the Llama-2-7b model as its base for continual learning tasks. It is evaluated in a series of training stages to assess its performance over time.|Here is another description: SSR with Llama-2-7b is a specific configuration of the Selective Sequence Replay (SSR) method, utilizing the Llama-2-7b model as its base language model. This setup is evaluated in the context of continual learning tasks to assess its performance against other baselines."},
{"ssr_with_llama_2_7b__fall_behind__randsel_10_in_terms_of_fwt_in_the_early_stage": "Falling behind in terms of FWT in the early stage indicates that SSR with Llama-2-7b initially performs less effectively than RandSel(10%) when measured by the FWT metric during the early phases of continual learning."},
{"randsel_10_in_terms_of_fwt_in_the_early_stage": "RandSel(10%) is a baseline method in continual learning that randomly selects 10% of the data for rehearsal. It is used as a comparison to evaluate the performance of SSR with Llama-2-7b, particularly in the early stages of learning where SSR initially underperforms in terms of FWT."},
{"ssr_with_llama_2_7b__strengthen__its_performance_as_the_number_of_training_stages_increases": "The predicate \"strengthen\" in this context refers to the gradual improvement or enhancement of SSR with Llama-2-7b's performance metrics as it undergoes more training stages in the continual learning process."},
{"its_performance_as_the_number_of_training_stages_increases": "The object \"its performance as the number of training stages increases\" describes the improvement in SSR with Llama-2-7b's effectiveness and results, which become more pronounced with each additional training stage in the continual learning sequence."},
