{"task_specific_ability": "Task-specific ability refers to the specialized skills or competencies that a language model (LLM) has developed for particular tasks. In this context, it pertains to the LLM's proficiency in handling the specific requirements and nuances of the 5 SuperNI tasks."},
{"task_specific_ability__evaluates__ar_performance_of_the_llm_on_5_superni_tasks": "The predicate \"evaluates\" indicates the process of assessing or measuring the performance of the LLM in relation to the 5 SuperNI tasks. This involves applying specific metrics or benchmarks to determine how well the LLM performs these tasks."},
