{"randsel_10_w_syn_op": "RandSel(10%) w/ syn. op. refers to a method where 10% of the data is randomly selected and synthetic operations are applied. This method is used in the context of continual learning with the Llama-2-7b model on SuperNI tasks.|Here is another description: RandSel(10%) w/ syn. op. represents a method where 10% of the inputs are randomly selected and synthetic outputs are applied. This technique is used in the continual learning process to enhance the performance of the model, as evidenced by the best BWT value of 0.02 achieved in CL order 3.|Here is another description: RandSel (10%) w/ syn. op. is a method used in experiments to evaluate the effectiveness of rehearsal techniques. It involves selecting a random 10% subset of previous instances for rehearsal purposes."},
