{"lightweight_strategies": "Lightweight strategies refer to methods or techniques designed to reduce the complexity or resource requirements of a system or model without significantly compromising its performance. These strategies are particularly valuable in applications where efficiency and speed are critical.|Here is another description: Lightweight strategies refer to methods or techniques designed to reduce the complexity or resource requirements of a model without significantly compromising its performance. These strategies are particularly valuable in scenarios where efficiency and speed are critical, such as in real-world applications involving large language models (LLMs)."},
