{"demonstrations_and_sampling": "Demonstrations and sampling refer to the processes of showcasing examples and selecting data points, respectively, which are crucial for generating synthetic instances in various applications."},
{"demonstrations_and_sampling__can_be_performed__multiple_times": "The ability to perform demonstrations and sampling multiple times indicates a flexible and iterative approach, allowing for the generation of diverse synthetic instances based on the base LLM _\u03b8_."},
{"multiple_times": "Performing demonstrations and sampling multiple times means repeating these processes several times to obtain a variety of synthetic instances, enhancing the robustness and diversity of the generated data."},
