{"base_llm__is_used__\u03b8_0": "The phrase \"is used\" indicates that the base LLM is actively employed or utilized in the process of obtaining different synthetic instances."},
{"icl_ability_of_llms": "The ICL (In-Context Learning) ability of LLMs (Large Language Models) refers to the capability of these models to learn and adapt to new tasks or information presented within the context of a given input, without the need for explicit retraining."},
{"icl_ability_of_llms__exhibits__significant_degradation_after_sft_on_specific_tasks": "The predicate \"exhibits\" indicates that the ICL ability of LLMs shows or displays a particular characteristic or behavior, in this case, a change in performance after undergoing a specific process."},
{"significant_degradation_after_sft_on_specific_tasks": "Significant degradation after SFT on specific tasks refers to a notable decline in the performance or effectiveness of the ICL ability of LLMs following supervised fine-tuning (SFT), which is a process of further training the model on a specific dataset to improve its performance on particular tasks."},
{"degradation_after_sft": "The degradation after supervised fine-tuning (SFT) refers to the decline in performance or capability of a language model following its fine-tuning on specific tasks."},
