{"continual_learning_sequence__starts_with__qa": "The predicate \"starts with\" indicates the initial task in the continual learning sequence. It signifies the beginning point of the sequence where the learning process commences."},
{"qa": "QA, or Question Answering, is the first task in the continual learning sequence. It involves training a model to generate answers to questions based on given contexts, serving as the starting point for the sequence of tasks.|Here is another description: QA is an entity within a sequence of operations or steps, positioned as the starting point in certain pathways.|Here is another description: QA is an entity or a state that SA transitions into, as per the directional relationship indicated by the predicate \u2192.|Here is another description: QA is an entity within a sequence of operations or processes, positioned as the starting point in the described context.|Here is another description: QA, following the Trans. entity in the sequence, likely represents a subsequent step or operation. It is an element that Trans. leads to or is associated with in the procedural flow.|Here is another description: QA appears to be an entity or state within a sequence of transitions or processes, possibly representing a quality assurance step in a workflow."},
{"continual_learning_sequence__followed_by__qg": "The predicate \"followed by\" indicates the sequential order in which tasks are conducted within the continual learning process. It signifies that one task is performed immediately after another in a predefined sequence."},
{"qg": "QG, or Question Generation, is one of the tasks in the continual learning sequence. It involves generating questions based on given contexts or passages, and it follows the QA (Question Answering) task in the specified order of the continual learning process.|Here is another description: QG is an entity that follows QA in a specific sequence or process, indicating a step or stage that comes after QA.|Here is another description: QG appears to be an entity or a step in a sequence, possibly representing a process or a stage in a series of operations or transformations.|Here is another description: QG is an entity that follows Sum. in the sequence, suggesting it is the next step or outcome resulting from the Sum. process or state.|Here is another description: QG appears to be an entity or a step in a sequence of operations or processes, as indicated by its position in the context."},
{"continual_learning_sequence__followed_by__sa": "The predicate \"followed by\" indicates the sequential order in which tasks are conducted within the continual learning process. It signifies that one task comes after another in a predefined sequence."},
