{"ssr__compares_with__multi_task_learning_mtl": "The predicate \"compares with\" indicates an evaluative process where SSR is being assessed in relation to other methods. This comparison likely involves metrics or performance indicators to determine the effectiveness or superiority of SSR over the baselines."},
{"multi_task_learning_mtl": "Multi-task Learning (MTL) is described as a commonly used baseline in the context. It involves training multiple tasks simultaneously, serving as a standard against which SSR is compared. MTL is likely a well-established method in the field of machine learning.|Here is another description: Multi-task Learning (MTL) is a machine learning approach where multiple tasks are trained simultaneously, allowing the model to learn shared representations that can improve performance across all tasks.|Here is another description: Multi-task Learning (MTL) is a machine learning approach where a model is trained to perform multiple tasks concurrently. It is often used as a baseline in experiments to compare the performance of different methods."},
