{"superni_tasks": "SuperNI tasks refer to a set of diverse and open-ended sequence generation tasks that require sophisticated evaluation metrics to assess performance."},
{"superni_tasks__adopt__rouge_l_metric": "The adoption of a specific metric, such as ROUGE-L, signifies the selection and implementation of this metric to evaluate the performance of language models on the given tasks."},
{"rouge_l_metric": "The ROUGE-L metric is a well-established evaluation metric used for assessing the quality of text summarization and other natural language generation tasks by measuring the longest common subsequence between the generated text and a reference text.|Here is another description: The ROUGE-L metric is a method used to assess the quality of text summarization and machine translation by comparing an automatically generated text with a reference text. It calculates the longest common subsequence between the two texts, providing a score that reflects their similarity.|Here is another description: The ROUGE-L metric is a method used to evaluate the performance of language models, particularly in tasks involving sequence generation. It is designed to measure the overlap between machine-generated text and human-generated text, providing a quantitative assessment of the model's output."},
{"rouge_l_metric__evaluate__performance_of_llm_on_each_task": "The predicate \"evaluate\" in this context refers to the action of assessing or measuring the effectiveness or quality of something, in this case, the performance of a Language Learning Model (LLM) on specific tasks using the ROUGE-L metric."},
{"performance_of_llm_on_each_task": "The performance of an LLM on each task refers to how well the Language Learning Model executes or completes the given tasks, which are likely related to text generation or summarization. This performance is quantified using the ROUGE-L metric to provide a numerical evaluation."},
