{"10_superni_tasks": "The 10 SuperNI tasks represent a set of specific machine learning challenges or benchmarks used to evaluate the performance of SSR and other baseline methods. These tasks are designed to test the capabilities of continual learning algorithms, providing a standard for comparison in terms of accuracy, robustness, and other relevant metrics.|Here is another description: The 10 SuperNI tasks refer to a set of specific natural language processing tasks that are used to evaluate the performance of language models like Llama-2-7b. These tasks likely cover a range of challenges and scenarios to thoroughly test the model's abilities."},
