{"llm__evaluated_from__three_perspectives": "The predicate \"evaluated from\" indicates the process of assessing the LLM's performance and capabilities from multiple angles or criteria. This evaluation is crucial to understand how well the LLM maintains its abilities after being fine-tuned and to compare its performance with other models or benchmarks."},
{"three_perspectives": "The object \"three perspectives\" refers to the different criteria or angles from which the LLM is being evaluated. These include the general instruction-following ability measured by AlpacaEval 2.0, the general language understanding ability assessed through the MMLU benchmark, and the task-specific ability evaluated on 5 SuperNI tasks. This multi-faceted evaluation helps in comprehensively understanding the LLM's capabilities and limitations."},
{"alpacaeval_2_0": "AlpacaEval 2.0 is a tool designed to assess the general instruction-following ability of language models. It measures performance based on a win rate comparison between the model's generations and those produced by a reference model, such as gpt-4-turbo."},
{"alpacaeval_2_0__used_as__automatic_evaluator": "The predicate \"used as\" indicates that AlpacaEval 2.0 serves a specific function or role within the context of evaluating language models. In this case, it is employed to automatically assess the instruction-following capabilities of a language model."},
{"automatic_evaluator": "An automatic evaluator is a system or tool that autonomously assesses the performance or capabilities of another system, in this context, a language model. AlpacaEval 2.0 functions as this automatic evaluator by comparing the model's outputs against a benchmark to determine its effectiveness in following instructions."},
{"llm_s_performance": "The performance of a large language model (LLM) in the context of continual learning and generalization ability, specifically focusing on its instruction-following capabilities as evaluated through automatic metrics."},
{"llm_s_performance__measured_in_terms_of__win_rate": "The evaluation of the LLM's performance is quantified by comparing its outputs to those of a benchmark model, gpt-4-turbo, using a specific metric that reflects its effectiveness in generating responses."},
{"win_rate": "The win rate is a metric used to measure the performance of an LLM, indicating the proportion of instances where the LLM's generated responses are preferred over those produced by gpt-4-turbo, as determined by an evaluation annotator like ChatGPT."},
{"llm_s_generations": "LLM\u2019s generations refer to the outputs produced by a language model, specifically in this context, the Alpaca-7b model after it has undergone continual learning on 5 SuperNI tasks and fine-tuning on the Alpaca-52k dataset. These generations are evaluated based on their instruction-following ability using AlpacaEval 2.0."},
{"llm_s_generations__compared_with__those_generated_by_gpt_4_turbo": "The predicate \"compared with\" indicates a process of evaluation where the outputs (generations) of the LLM (Alpaca-7b) are assessed against a benchmark or standard. In this case, the comparison is made to determine how well the LLM\u2019s generations perform relative to those produced by another model, specifically gpt-4-turbo."},
{"those_generated_by_gpt_4_turbo": "The object \"those generated by gpt-4-turbo\" refers to the outputs produced by the gpt-4-turbo model, which serve as a benchmark for evaluating the performance of the LLM\u2019s (Alpaca-7b) generations. The comparison is made to assess the win rate of the LLM in terms of general instruction-following ability."},
