{"evaluation_annotator": "An evaluation annotator is a tool or system used to assess and provide feedback on the performance of another system, typically in the context of natural language processing or machine learning. In this context, it is used to compare the generations of the LLM with those generated by gpt-4-turbo."},
{"mmlu_benchmark": "The MMLU benchmark is a standardized test designed to assess the general language understanding capabilities of language models. It covers a wide range of topics and is used to evaluate how well a model can comprehend and generate natural language."},
{"mmlu_benchmark__used_for__evaluating_general_language_understanding_ability": "The predicate \"used for\" indicates the purpose or function of the MMLU benchmark within the context of evaluating language models. It signifies that the benchmark serves as a tool or method to measure specific abilities or performance metrics."},
