{"practical_in_real_world_applications": "Being \"practical in real-world applications\" means that a method or approach is feasible, efficient, and effective when implemented in actual, everyday scenarios. In the context of machine learning models, practicality often involves considerations like inference time, resource usage, and overall performance in operational environments."},
{"inference_time_of_llms": "The inference time of LLMs (Large Language Models) refers to the duration it takes for these models to process and generate responses or outputs after receiving input. This metric is essential in evaluating the efficiency and practicality of deploying LLMs in various applications."},
{"inference_time_of_llms__is_a_crucial_consideration__in_real_world_applications": "Being a crucial consideration means that the inference time of LLMs is a significant factor that must be taken into account when deploying these models in practical, real-world scenarios. Efficient inference time is vital for ensuring that LLMs can operate within acceptable performance limits and meet the demands of users."},
