{"task_agnostic_representation_consolidation": "Task agnostic representation consolidation refers to a method designed to integrate and maintain knowledge across different tasks without being biased towards any specific task. It aims to create a versatile and adaptable learning system that can effectively handle continual learning scenarios."},
{"task_agnostic_representation_consolidation__is__a_self_supervised_based_continual_learning_approach": "The term \"is\" in this context signifies that the subject, task agnostic representation consolidation, is being defined or characterized as a particular type of approach. It serves as a linking verb to equate the subject with the object, providing clarity on the nature of the method."},
{"a_self_supervised_based_continual_learning_approach": "A self-supervised based continual learning approach is a technique where the system learns continuously from new data without requiring explicit labels. It leverages self-supervision to generate its own labels from the data, allowing it to adapt and improve over time in a task-agnostic manner."},
